  "2026-11-16T07:29:06.075Z",codex-sol,"Round K: PRRT_kwDOVLY-P863zl6f verified and fixed. The deadline inventory now recursively recognizes object/array/default/rest bindings, catch parameters, variable/function/class declarations and named expressions. Twenty shadowing forms each have a rejection control and a renamed binding control; property keys alone retain helper credit. Required gates passed through pm test: npm run typecheck; npm run lint; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/review-close-contracts.test.ts test/coverage-aggregation.test.ts test/ci-routing.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts; git diff --check. Combined suite: 18 passed, zero failed/skipped. Tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the successful execution receipt. No thread mutations. Releasing in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-16T08:24:19.652Z",codex-sol,"Review round L: verify supplied findings against code, apply scoped fixes, run local gates and linked regression evidence, then release without closing. No review-thread replies or resolution."
  "2026-11-16T08:26:51.029Z",codex-sol,"Regenerated with npm run changelog:full. CHANGELOG.md diff is exactly four added lines: the Other heading and pm-swarm-ci-extension-host-skew entry. Typecheck, lint and all eight changelog bridge/routing/workflow tests passed in the linked snapshot. The subsequent changelog check could not locate Git metadata in the snapshot; run that tag-dependent gate directly in the package worktree."
  "2026-11-16T08:30:43.886Z",codex-sol,"Round L complete: failing test (26) changelog gate fixed by regenerating CHANGELOG.md with npm run changelog:full. Verified the only changelog diff is the requested Other entry. Final linked gate passed typecheck, lint and all eight changelog bridge/CI routing/release workflow tests, zero failures/skips. Direct npm run changelog:check and git diff --check passed. The initial snapshot changelog attempt failed only because snapshots omit Git metadata; the corrected linked entry excludes that Git-dependent command. Releasing in progress; no merges, closes or thread mutations."
